 "document": {
  "id": "D03",
  "path": "conversations/conv_pines016_shelf_space.eml",
  "text": "From: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Shelf space vs. usage - help needed\nDate: Mon, 13 Apr 2009 10:15:00 -0500\n\nQuestion for the group: How do I figure out if I'm using my shelf space\nefficiently? I need something that shows me, for each genre and format:\n- What percentage of total circulations it has\n- What percentage of the collection it is\n- What percentage of total shelf space it occupies\n\nDoes anyone else need this?\n\nMaria\nP.S. Does anyone know if the new Marvel movie is any good?\n===\nFrom: thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Shelf space vs. usage - help needed\nDate: Mon, 13 Apr 2009 11:02:33 -0500\n\nYES, I need this too. As a cataloger, I'm always trying to convince our\ndirector to reallocate space from low-circulation genres to high-circulation\nones. Having actual data would be game-changing.\n\nCurrently I pull reports manually and make spreadsheets. It's tedious.\n\nMy kid is obsessed with dinosaur books right now. I'm reading \"The Rise and\nFall of the Dinosaurs\" at bedtime. Apparently T-Rex could bite through a\ncar. Fascinating bedtime reading.\n===\nFrom: susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Shelf space vs. usage - help needed\nDate: Mon, 13 Apr 2009 11:45:07 -0500\n\nThis is the \"shelf space report\" we've been talking about. The idea is:\nfor each genre and format of material, compare:\n1. Percentage of total circulations\n2. Percentage of the collection\n3. Percentage of total shelf space\n\nThe report should be able to run per library and per system. This way branch\nmanagers can see their local situation AND see how they compare to the system\naverage.\n\nI just got back from the farmer's market. Got some amazing heirloom tomatoes.\nAnyone tried making a tomato sandwich with just basil, salt, and bread?\nHeaven on earth.\n===\nFrom: latoya.davidson@twinlakeslib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org, susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Shelf space vs. usage - help needed\nDate: Mon, 13 Apr 2009 12:30:55 -0500\n\nI would need this at the system level for sure. When I look at Twin Lakes\nas a whole, we might have too many romance novels in some branches and not\nenough in others. Being able to redistribute based on data would help.\n\nCan we also filter by date range? Like, what was the shelf space utilization\nin Q1 vs. Q2? Seasons matter for our collection.\n\nAlso, my cat Mittens keeps knocking plants off my windowsill. I've moved the\nplants but he finds new ones to knock over. Cats are ridiculous.\n===\nFrom: robert.chen@gapubliclib.org\nTo: latoya.davidson@twinlakeslib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Shelf space vs. usage - help needed\nDate: Mon, 13 Apr 2009 14:10:22 -0500\n\nFrom a data perspective, we need to:\n1. Count items per genre/format (this is the \"percentage of collection\")\n2. Sum checkouts per genre/format (this is the \"percentage of circulations\")\n3. Estimate shelf space per genre/format (this is the \"percentage of shelf space\")\n\nThe tricky part is #3. Shelf space isn't directly tracked in the database.\nWe'd need to estimate based on item dimensions or use item count as a proxy.\n\nWe can also add the per-library and per-system breakdown. That's just\nadding GROUP BY clauses to the right levels.\n\nGoing to try that pesto recipe I found. Using the basil from my garden.\n===\nFrom: jennifer.durham@statesboro.lib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org, susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org, latoya.davidson@twinlakeslib.org, robert.chen@gapubliclib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Shelf space vs. usage - help needed\nDate: Mon, 13 Apr 2009 15:20:00 -0500\n\nI want this broken down per library AND per system. Our directors review\nthis data quarterly and need both views.\n\nAlso, can we include a \"comparison\" view that shows each library's breakdown\nside by side? That would make it easy to spot outliers.\n\nMy sister is visiting from Atlanta this weekend. She's been begging me to\ntake her to Callaway Gardens. I haven't been since I was a kid.\n===\nFrom: katherine.gregory@gapubliclib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: SUMMARY: Shelf space report requirement\nDate: Tue, 14 Apr 2009 08:30:00 -0500\n\nGreat discussion everyone. Summarizing the Shelf Space Report requirement:\n\nThe system should provide, for each genre and format of material, the ability\nto compare:\n- The percentage of total circulations\n- The percentage of the collection\n- The percentage of total shelf space\n\nThe report should be available per library and per system.\n\nAction items:\n- Robert will investigate how to estimate shelf space from existing data\n- Susan will coordinate with branch managers for testing\n\nI need to buy new running shoes. These old ones are falling apart.\n\n-Katherine"
 },
 "requirements": [
