  "text": "From: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Volume reporting - how do we count what we have?\nDate: Mon, 06 Apr 2009 08:42:11 -0500\n\nHi everyone,\n\nQuick question - how do I get a report that tells me how many items we have\nat Dalton-Whitman at any given moment? Not just total count, but broken down\nby categories. Like total items in library, number of holds, number of adult\nfiction, number of board books...\n\nWe need this for our monthly board report and I'm currently pulling it\nmanually from three different screens. :(\n\n-Maria\n===\nFrom: george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Volume reporting - how do we count what we have?\nDate: Mon, 06 Apr 2009 09:15:23 -0500\n\nMaria, are you getting the volume based on what's currently checked in?\nI assume items that are checked out still count toward your total volume,\nright? Just asking because the distinction matters for how we design this.\n\nAlso - did anyone see that Pies 'n' Thighs is opening a second location?\nMy wife is already planning our anniversary dinner there.\n===\nFrom: susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Volume reporting - how do we count what we have?\nDate: Mon, 06 Apr 2009 10:03:45 -0500\n\nYes, George has a good point. The volume should include:\n1. New acquisitions (items recently added)\n2. Items on the shelf (checked in)\n3. Items out in circulation (checked out)\n\nI think Maria is asking for all three counts separately plus a total. That\nmakes sense for collection management.\n\nAlso, the breakdown by categories is important. We need things like:\n- Total items\n- Number of holds\n- Number of adult fiction\n- Number of board books\n- Maybe other categories too\n\nMy daughter has her recital tomorrow and I'm trying not to think about work\nbut here we are. :P\n===\nFrom: latoya.davidson@twinlakeslib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org, susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Volume reporting - how do we count what we have?\nDate: Mon, 06 Apr 2009 11:20:01 -0500\n\nI second this request. At Twin Lakes we need this for our quarterly\nassessment. Can we make the categories customizable? Different libraries\nmight want different breakdowns.\n\nAlso, Robert - any idea if the database tracks acquisition date? It would\nbe helpful to see how much volume has been added in the last 30/60/90 days.\n\nBTW, anyone know a good restaurant in Athens? I'm taking my mom out for\nher birthday dinner this weekend.\n===\nFrom: robert.chen@gapubliclib.org\nTo: latoya.davidson@twinlileslib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Volume reporting - how do we count what we have?\nDate: Mon, 06 Apr 2009 14:33:22 -0500\n\nLatoya (note: typo in your email address) -\n\nYes, the database tracks acquisition date for items. We can definitely\nbuild reports that show volume changes over time.\n\nFor the volume report, I'm thinking we need a query that:\n1. Counts all items with a location = your library\n2. Groups by categories (fiction/non-fiction, format, etc.)\n3. Shows breakdowns with holds count per category\n\nWe can also add date filters - volume at any point in time, not just\ncurrent. This would be useful for historical comparisons.\n\nI'm heading to the Braves game tonight with some colleagues. Go Braves!\n===\nFrom: katherine.gregory@gapubliclib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: SUMMARY: Volume reporting discussion\nDate: Tue, 07 Apr 2009 08:15:00 -0500\n\nThanks everyone for the input. Here's what I'm hearing for the \"Material\nVolume Report\" requirement:\n\nThe system should provide the ability to report on the volume of material\nin a given library at any point in time, based on:\n- New acquisitions\n- Items on the shelf (checked in)\n- Items out in circulation (checked out)\n\nThe report should allow breaking down volume in categories such as:\n- Total items in library\n- Number of holds\n- Number of adult fiction\n- Number of board books\n- Other customizable categories\n\nThis will be tracked as a key requirement.\n\nAlso, I need coffee. Real coffee. Not the office sludge.\n\n- Katherine"
 },
