 "document": {
  "id": "D07",
  "path": "conversations/conv_pines022_deletions.eml",
  "text": "From: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Tracking deletions - who deleted what?\nDate: Fri, 24 Apr 2009 10:00:00 -0500\n\nQuick question: Is there a way to track when records are deleted? We need\nto be able to count and track record deletions (item records, patron\nrecords) per location and per system. This is for auditing purposes.\n\nRight now when something gets deleted, it just... disappears. No record.\n\nMaria\n===\nFrom: george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Tracking deletions - who deleted what?\nDate: Fri, 24 Apr 2009 10:45:33 -0500\n\nYes, we absolutely need this. Last month our director asked for a report\nof all patron records deleted in Q1 and I had to piece it together from\nmemory and email logs. Not professional.\n\nWe need:\n- What type of record was deleted (item/patron/bib)\n- When it was deleted\n- Who deleted it\n- Where they were located (which branch)\n- Possibly why (status before deletion?)\n\nMy neighbor just got a new puppy. It's a golden doodle named Biscuit.\nApparently Biscuit has a taste for garden hose.\n\n-George\n===\nFrom: robert.chen@gapubliclib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Tracking deletions - who deleted what?\nDate: Fri, 24 Apr 2009 11:30:00 -0500\n\nThis is actually a good idea from an auditing standpoint. Currently,\nEvergreen does not log deletions - once something is deleted, it's gone.\n\nTo implement this, we'd need:\n1. A trigger in the database that logs deletions to an audit table\n2. Fields: record_type, record_id, deleted_by, deleted_at, location\n3. A report interface to query this audit table\n\nThe report should show deletions per location and per system. We can\naggregate by date range, by user, by record type.\n\nMy laptop battery is at 2%. I need to plug in before I lose this draft.\n===\nFrom: dana.peeler@ohoopeelib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org, robert.chen@gapubliclib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Tracking deletions - who deleted what?\nDate: Fri, 24 Apr 2009 12:15:00 -0500\n\nI agree with George - this is about accountability. If we accidentally\ndelete something we shouldn't have, we need to be able to trace it.\n\nAlso, the deletion log would help with troubleshooting. \"Why did this\npatron's record disappear?\" - check the log.\n\nTaking my daughter to ballet class. She has a recital next week and\nis very nervous.\n\n-Dana\n===\nFrom: susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org, robert.chen@gapubliclib.org, dana.peeler@ohoopeelib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Tracking deletions - who deleted what?\nDate: Fri, 24 Apr 2009 13:40:00 -0500\n\nFrom an administrative perspective, we need reports showing:\n- Total deletions per period (month, quarter, year)\n- Deletions by type (item vs patron vs other)\n- Deletions by location\n- Top users who delete the most records\n\nThis helps us identify if certain branches are deleting more than others,\nwhich might indicate a process issue.\n\nI'm reading \"Where the Crawdads Sing\" right now. The marsh descriptions\nare beautiful.\n\n-Susan\n===\nFrom: latoya.davidson@twinlakeslib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org, robert.chen@gapubliclib.org, dana.peeler@ohoopeelib.org, susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Tracking deletions - who deleted what?\nDate: Fri, 24 Apr 2009 14:25:00 -0500\n\nThis also helps with compliance. Some libraries need to prove they're\nhandling data according to retention schedules. Being able to show\n\"we deleted 500 patron records on X date\" is important for audits.\n\nCan we also track attempted deletions that were denied? That would tell\nus if someone is trying to delete things they shouldn't.\n\nTrying out a new recipe for chicken tikka masala tonight. Fingers crossed.\n===\nFrom: katherine.gregory@gapubliclib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: SUMMARY: Deletion tracking requirement\nDate: Mon, 27 Apr 2009 09:00:00 -0500\n\nRequirement consolidated:\n\nThe system should count and track record deletions (e.g., item records,\npatron records) per location and per system. Tracking should include:\n- Record type\n- Timestamp\n- User who performed the deletion\n- Location of the user\n\nAdditionally, tracking of denied deletion attempts would be helpful for\ncompliance and troubleshooting.\n\nRobert will implement the database triggers. Katherine will draft the\nreport interface requirements.\n\nNow I need to find that chicken tikka recipe...\n\n-Katherine"
 },
 "requirements": [
  {
   "index": 1,
   "name": "Current Last-Copy Reports",
   "description": "The system must provide reports identifying Items that are the only copy within a selected scope, including an individual Branch and the entire Consortium."
  },
  {
   "index": 2,
   "name": "Administer Report Permissions",
   "description": "The system must provide fine-grained, role-administered permissions controlling who may create, clone, run, and access reports. Administrators must be able to create shared folders that allow or disallow access to specific reports and ad hoc reports on specified data sets."
  },
  {
   "index": 3,
   "name": "Assistive Technology Access",
   "description": "The system must support screen readers, screen-magnification software, and other assistive technologies, including JAWS, NVDA, and ZoomText, and comply with Section 508 accessibility requirements."
  },
  {
   "index": 4,
   "name": "Client Access Platforms and Browsers",
   "description": "The system must be accessible through a web browser or a Windows-compatible client; when accessed through a web browser, it must support Microsoft Internet Explorer version 6.0 or later and Mozilla Firefox version 2.0 or later."
  },
  {
   "index": 5,
   "name": "Consortium Scale Support",
