{
 "document": {
  "id": "D04",
  "path": "conversations/conv_pines018_item_transfer.eml",
  "text": "From: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Moving items between branches - utility needed\nDate: Mon, 11 May 2009 09:00:00 -0500\n\nI need a utility for transferring batches of items between branches. We\noften need to move books to a mobile library, to an outreach program, or\nto a \"just-in-time\" warehouse.\n\nThe utility needs:\n- Query for candidate materials\n- Save queries for repeated use\n- Manually select titles from query results\n- Change records of selected items to new location\n- Mechanisms: changing location field, generating pull lists\n- Revert items to original location after a set period of time\n\nWho else needs this?\n\nMaria\n(My neighbor's fence fell down in the storm. I loaned them my ladder.\nGood fences make good neighbors... but broken fences make good neighborly\ninteractions.)\n===\nFrom: thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Moving items between branches - utility needed\nDate: Mon, 11 May 2009 09:45:00 -0500\n\nWe need this in cataloging all the time. We transfer items between our\nbranches for collection balancing and for special programs.\n\nThe \"save queries for repeated use\" is crucial. We do this monthly - move\nall items in genre X that haven't circulated in 6 months.\n\nAlso, the \"revert items to original location after a set period of time\"\nis important for temporary transfers. For example, we send items to a\nbook sale for 30 days, then they need to come back.\n\nCan we also revert \"based on other criteria\"? Like, if the item's status\nchanges to \"sold\" at the book sale, automatically revert it?\n\nMy cat has started bringing me \"gifts\" - namely, socks he's stolen from\nthe laundry. He's very proud of himself.\n===\nFrom: robert.chen@gapubliclib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Moving items between branches - utility needed\nDate: Mon, 11 May 2009 10:30:00 -0500\n\nFrom a technical standpoint, this is doable but requires careful design.\nThe key components:\n\n1. Query builder for candidate selection - we can reuse the report query\n   tool for this.\n\n2. Save/share queries - similar to report templates.\n\n3. Batch update of location field - straightforward database update with\n   transaction safety.\n\n4. Pull list generation - create a printable list of items to be moved.\n\n5. Auto-revert mechanism - a scheduled task that checks transferred items\n   and reverts them based on time or status criteria.\n\n6. Logging - track all transfers for audit purposes.\n\nOne concern: with 9.6 million items, batch updates need to be efficient.\nWe should process in smaller batches to avoid locking the database.\n\nMy coffee maker broke this morning. Had to use the office coffee.\nSurvival mode activated.\n===\nFrom: george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org, robert.chen@gapubliclib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Moving items between branches - utility needed\nDate: Mon, 11 May 2009 11:15:00 -0500\n\nI like the auto-revert based on criteria. For example:\n- Revert after X days (date-based)\n- Revert when item status changes to \"returned\" (event-based)\n- Revert when item is checked out at the destination (event-based)\n\nThe event-based reversion is tricky but very useful. We send items to\na mobile library, and when they're checked out there, they should stay.\nBut if they just sit there unused, they come back.\n\nAlso, can we generate transit labels? Like, printable barcodes for the\nitems being transferred?\n\nWatching \"Chef's Table\" again. That episode with the Danish pastry chef\nis mesmerizing.\n===\nFrom: susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org, robert.chen@gapubliclib.org, george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Moving items between branches - utility needed\nDate: Mon, 11 May 2009 12:00:00 -0500\n\nWe need to be careful about permissions here. Not every staff member\nshould be able to transfer items between branches. This should be limited\nto certain roles (managers, administrators, transfer coordinators).\n\nAlso, the utility should show a preview before making changes. \"If you\nrun this now, 25 items will be moved from Dalton-Whitman to Mobile\nLibrary Unit 3. Confirm?\"\n\nAnd we need an undo function! What if someone clicks the wrong button?\n\nMy daughter's goldfish died. She's devastated. We're getting a new one\nnamed Bubbles II.\n===\nFrom: jennifer.durham@statesboro.lib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org, robert.chen@gapubliclib.org, george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org, susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Moving items between branches - utility needed\nDate: Mon, 11 May 2009 13:30:00 -0500\n\nI also want to be able to MANUALLY SELECT from query results. Maybe I\nrun a query and get 100 candidate items, but I only want to move 25 of\nthem. I should be able to check boxes and select which ones to include.\n\nAnd can we set up alerts? If an item transfer is delayed or has issues,\nnotify me.\n\nWe had a power outage at the library yesterday. 30 minutes. Felt like\nbeing in the stone age.\n\n-Jenny\n===\nFrom: latoya.davidson@twinlakeslib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, thomas.wright@augusta-reed.lib.org, robert.chen@gapubliclib.org, george.tuttle@piedmontlib.org, susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org, jennifer.durham@statesboro.lib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Moving items between branches - utility needed\nDate: Mon, 11 May 2009 14:15:00 -0500\n\nCan we track transfer history? Like, \"this item has been transferred 5\ntimes in the past year.\" That might indicate a problem with the item\nbeing in the wrong location.\n\nAlso, for the outreach program use case - can we transfer items to a\ntemporary location for a specific event or program? Like, move 20 biographies\nto the community center for their genealogy workshop, then revert them\nafter the event.\n\nMy mom bought a new vacuum cleaner. It's so powerful it picked up our\ncat's tail. He ran around the house like a tumbleweed.\n===\nFrom: katherine.gregory@gapubliclib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: SUMMARY: Item transfer utility requirement\nDate: Tue, 12 May 2009 09:00:00 -0500\n\nMajor requirement consolidated:\n\nThe system should provide a utility for transferring batches of items\nbetween branches. This includes:\n\n- Ability to query for candidate materials\n- Ability to save queries for repeated use\n- Ability to manually select titles from query results\n- Ability to change records of selected items to move to new location\n- Mechanisms: changing location field, generating pull lists\n- Ability to revert items to original location after a set period of time\n  and/or based on other criteria\n\nAdditional features requested:\n- Preview before making changes\n- Undo function\n- Permission control (limited to managers/admins)\n- Transfer history tracking\n- Event-based and time-based auto-revert\n- Printable transit labels\n- Transfer delay alerts\n\nAction: Robert will investigate technical constraints. Thomas will\ncoordinate testing with cataloging staff.\n\n-Katherine\n(P.S. Bubbles II will be fine, Susan. Goldfish have a 3-second memory.\n...Wait, that's a myth. They actually remember things for months.)"
 },
